Author: Maximilian Smidt <134879273+maxi-smidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 21 09:45:12 2026 +0000

    fix(tree-view): apply token/year search matching to current-tree canvas search

    The tree canvas search box's "current tree" results for a normally
    loaded (non-windowed) tree are filtered client-side with
    getMemberSearchText().includes(query) — a plain whole-string substring
    check that never picked up the new tokenized/year-aware matching from
    member_name_search_clause. This made a member findable via the
    cross-tree "other trees" section (backed by the server) but not from
    their own currently open tree for the same reordered or year-appended
    query.

    Add memberMatchesSearch() as a client-side mirror of the backend
    matching rules and use it for the client-filtered path.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 69224aa20196

